  description: About Toronto Trees, an interactive map of every street tree in the city.
  og_image: /og-default.png

options: null

content:
  heading: About
  paragraphs[3]:
    - "Toronto Trees is an interactive map of every documented street tree in the city, well over a half-million of them, visualized from open data. Each point represents one tree, coloured by genus and sized by trunk diameter. This project was created because there wasn't a clear place to find this information in the most intuitive medium for it: a map."
    - "The data comes from the city's urban forestry data, updated every quarter. Only trees on public road allowances are included; private, park, and ravine trees are limited this dataset. If you happen to know how to access all city park trees, please reach out."
    - "Send feedback on this site via <a href=\"https://github.com/orvn/toronto-trees\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub</a>."
